1. Lemma 9.1 on 279 random PD tridiagonal matrices (n = 2..12, mixed signs): pivots all > 0; max |sum of blocks - H| = 4.4e-16; min relative block eigenvalue = -1.2e-16; max relative |det| = 2.0e-16
2. Consequence A: clique-PSD bound vs exact QP minimum on 24 random sub-boxes (n = 4, c = 0 or random, uniform or mixed signs of b): max |difference| = 4.0e-08
3. Balanced split, kappa = 0.1: interior factor convex on the centred cube iff t <= 0.577350 (1/sqrt(3) = 0.577350); end factors iff t <= 0.850798; interior factor at (1, 1): lambda_min = -0.400; interior factor at (0.775, 0): lambda_min = -0.0002 (the convex set of a factor is not a cube)
4. Convexity / Frank-Wolfe validity on 300 random boxes, n = 5: abb: min Hessian eigenvalue of the relaxation = 1.121, max (FW bound - minimum) = -3.6e-02; abbU: min Hessian eigenvalue of the relaxation = 0.533, max (FW bound - minimum) = 1.1e-16; abbS: min Hessian eigenvalue of the relaxation = 0.056, max (FW bound - minimum) = 2.2e-16
